\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid3932697 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid3932697 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
Reality is a much-debated topic, and has been for many years through out history.  Countless numbers of philosophers as well as scientists have tackled the question of what makes up our surroundings and what accounts for the entire phenomenon that we perc
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 e\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
ive.  From multiple dimensions of existence, to theories of quantum mechanics and relativity, there have been many attempts to define this reality with precision and truth.  What it seems to be is a conceptual organization of thoughts and definitions base
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 d\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 on observations made by each individual.  This leads us not only to an objective reality that follows certain rules according to an observer, but also to a subjective reality that can bend and change according to the will of the observer.  These two side
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 s\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 have been chosen independently of each other for centuries and argued against each other.  Unfortunately, when you use reality to argue against itself, you can no longer reach factual or plausible conclusions, as you cannot use half of something to defin
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 e\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 the whole.  You can, however, use the two opposite sides of reality to define each other, and therefore the whole.  In this sense, using objective definitions and subjective decisions, you can conceivably reach an accurate model of reality.  All you need
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 to begin is a probable structure.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
Here, I will be getting into a field of science known as quantum mechanics, or sub-atomic particle physics.  While this is known as an extremely complicated field, employing advanced mathematics, I assure you that you will not need any of that here.  You 
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 s\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 \hich\f0 ee, I will be working with the philosophies behind each of the theories here, and so the math will be really inconsequential.  I am interested in the \'93\loch\f0 \hich\f0 why\'94
\loch\f0 \hich\f0  of quantum mechanics, not the \'93\loch\f0 \hich\f0 how.\'94\loch\f0   Through the exploration and application of these concepts and\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
philosophies.  I intend on outlining an existence where all possibilities are occurring, and where the version of existence you are perceiving is based solely upon the conscious choices of each observer involved.
\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 There is a philosophical idea that attempts\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 to describe existence and the number of possibilities that exist.  It has implications in the concept of destiny and fate, and can be used to support the concept that everything is possible.  Any idea that can be conceived by a consciousness has a probab
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 i\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
lity of not only existing, but occurring.  It comes down to the decisions that each consciousness makes, as it is the decisions that create the interference in the infinite interactions of energy waves which ultimately make up the reality we perceive.  It
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 is known as the Multiverse, and has many startling yet supporting theories in the field of quantum mechanics.  It all started one day, when someone noticed the dual nature of the particle.  
