\par \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 It is this concept of observation and mea\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
surement that has become one of the great unresolved questions of Quantum Mechanics.  It is this concept of observation and choice that will be the key to defining your ability to bend and shape reality around your will though, as apparently it is your de
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 c\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 isions in focusing your observations that defines when energy becomes matter.
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs20\insrsid3932697 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 Matter is Energy and Energy is Matter
\par 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \fi720\li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid3932697 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
"Today, young people are beginning to realize that matter is nothing but enery reduced to a slow vibration." (Bill Hicks)  This was one of\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 the more fantastic and tantalizing concepts that had yet come upon the field of science.  Matter is energy and energy is matter.  It's state however, depends on when an observation is made.  Imagine that?  Energy, all energy is "floating around" in wave 
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 f\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
orm until an observation is made, either on a conscious or unconscious level.  Until you (and albeit everyone else at the same time) look up and notice that there is a tree there, all the matter that makes up that tree is just a collection of waves of ene
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 r\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
gy.  How this energy is defined at any given point is completely up to the perceptions of the observer.  Completely contingent on the fact that you are indeed observing it and the energy surrounding it.  As you become more familiar (from birth on) with th
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 e\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
 different forms that energy takes, you begin to call them objects.  You are able to give them shapes, sounds, smells, tastes and textures according to the observations made using your perceptions.  You are able to (at least on the level of classical phys
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 i\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
cs) define most everything about these energy forms, as we are dealing with a macroscopic level of particles.  However, when we begin to look at things on a sub-atomic level, on the supermicroscopic level of particles, we are no longer obliged by the simp
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 l\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
icity of observing waveforms of energy.  Here, light does not even act like light anymore.  It is no longer a reflecting wave of electromagnetic energy, rather it is a collection of photons all acting according to the laws of quantum mechanics.  In classi
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 c\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 
al physics, you are able to point to a location and say what it is that you observe existing there.  In quantum mechanics, you can point to a location and say what it is that you observe that has a tendency to exist, as particles do indeed have a tendency
\hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 to exist.  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs20\insrsid3932697 \hich\af0\dbch\af31505\loch\f0 (MORE)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\insrsid3932697 
